# SAM 3 reference golden: the full high-res encoder pyramid (~38 MB at the model's
# fixed 1008 internal resolution) is too large to commit; it is regenerable via
# tests/parity/reference_sam3/capture_sam3_golden.py. The small image.npz / video.npz
# golden fixtures ARE committed.
tests/parity/fixtures/sam3/image_encoder_pyramid.npz
# SAM 3.1 multiplex golden: the full BUCKET-SPACE frame-1 decode (trk_f1_mux_buckets,
# ~8 MB; num_buckets x K=16 slots incl. padding) is bulky and regenerable. The committed
# video_sam31.npz keeps the essentials (per-object demux + mux/demux mapping). Regenerate
# via: capture_sam3_golden.py --model sam3.1.
tests/parity/fixtures/sam3/video_sam31_multiplex_internals.npz
# Throwaway capture scratch (smoke/verify scripts, re-run dir) — never committed.
tests/parity/reference_sam3/_*.py
tests/parity/reference_sam3/_rerun/

